Data Curation Details
The data was curated from the tmQMg dataset by Kneiding et al.(1)
Bond threshold is inferred using the sum of covalent radii between two atoms,(2) the standard deviation, and a constant 0.225 (which is based on half of the 0.45 constant from Rasmussen et al. to account for the standard deviation)(3), with the exact formula:
RA + RB + k(√(〖σ_A〗^2+〖σ_B〗^2 )) +0.225
The k chosen was 3 to reflect the normal distribution that covers up to 99.7% data points
Exclusion list:
	Seat size not 5 or 6
	Seat not a cyclic ring
	Anionic complexes
	Leg number not 3
	π or σ ligands as leg ligands
	carborane ligands
	oxidation state (detected from SMILES provided in the tmQMg dataset) > 5
	rhodium and iridium with six membered arene rings
	tridentate legs
	certain rings with missing hydrogen
	fulvenes (by applying C-C distance < 1.425 and not in a fused aromatic ring)
	cyclopentadienone and related compounds (anything with oxygen having only 1 neighbour according to the graph)
	bidentate legs with complex chelate ring system (can be defined as having multiple chelate rings of similar size)
Featurization Details
Alignment of coordinates was done using the Kabsch algorithm
